  m_Name: device-tiering
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: GameTerms.Runtime::GameTerms.GlossaryTermAsset
  data:
    Id: device-tiering
    Term: Device Tiering
    Abbreviation: 
    Category: 6
    Difficulty: 1
    ShortDefinition: Grouping target hardware into performance classes with matching
      quality presets.
    SimpleExplanation: Sorting phones into low, mid, and high settings buckets.
    WhyItMatters: Tiering lets one build serve a wide audience without overtaxing
      weak devices.
    Example: Low tier disables shadows and caps particles while high tier enables
      them.
    CommonMistake: Shipping one quality preset for all phones and failing on older
      hardware.
    PracticePrompt: Define three tiers with concrete feature flags and map five devices
      into them.
    GameUses:
    - Quality settings
    - Market coverage
    - Performance QA
    RelatedTermIds:
    - adaptive-performance
    - dynamic-resolution
    - thermal-throttling
    Tags:
    - devices
    - quality
    - mobile
    Synonyms: []
